; error: 11:5: 'setCopy' copies a 'T' into region 'local' at 4:15, and 'local' is declared inside 'setCopy' and freed when it ends, so that copy is only the value itself; this use gives text@outer, which is in region 'outer'. So copy the value before the call, or write 'setCopy' for text@outer itself
task setCopy<T>(flex xs: [T]@r, v: T)
    region local
    xs[0] = v.copy() at local
fi

task main()
    region outer
    flex xs: [text@outer]@outer = new [text](["x"]) at outer
    fixed s: text@outer = "hello".copy() at outer
    setCopy(xs, s)
    show(xs[0])
fi
